e>Hagberg</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hickson</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ehsani</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Holloszy</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Faster adjustment to and recovery from submaximal exercise in the trained state</article-title><source>J Appl Physiol</source><year>1980</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>218</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7364606</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kirby</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartung</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Briefly: heart rate deceleration in conditioned and unconditioned men</article-title><source>Am Correct Ther J</source><year>1980</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>162</fpage><lpage>163</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7211649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darr</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bassett</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of age and training status on heart rate recovery after peak exercise</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1988</year><volume>254</volume><fpage>H340</fpage><lpage>H343</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3344824</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>